      {"t":"mc","q":"Which word goes before a first name as a polite title?","o":["คุณ","ครับ","ค่ะ","ไหม"],"why":"คุณ + first name, as in คุณมาลี, for men and women."},
      {"t":"order","p":"Sorry. (female speaker)","a":["ขอโทษ","ค่ะ"],"x":["คะ"],"why":"In a statement ค่ะ has a falling tone; คะ with a high tone is for questions."},
      {"t":"order","p":"How are you? (female speaker)","a":["สบาย","ดี","ไหม","คะ"],"x":["ค่ะ"],"why":"A question ends in คะ, with a high tone; ค่ะ, with a falling tone, ends statements."},
      {"t":"order","p":"Nice to meet you. (male speaker)","a":["ยินดี","ที่","ได้","รู้จัก","ครับ"],"x":["ค่ะ"],"why":"A man ends with ครับ, even after a long phrase; ค่ะ is what women say."},
      {"t":"fill","q":"ขอบคุณ__","p":"Thank you. (female speaker)","a":["ค่ะ","khâ"],"o":["คะ","ครับ","ไหม"],"why":"A woman ends a statement with ค่ะ, falling; คะ is for questions.","xr":["khá","khráp","mǎi"]},
      {"t":"fill","q":"สบายดีไหม__","p":"How are you? (female speaker)","a":["คะ","khá"],"o":["ค่ะ","ครับ","นะ"],"why":"After ไหม a woman uses คะ, with a high tone.","xr":["khâ","khráp","ná"]},
      {"t":"fill","q":"__ครับ","p":"It's OK. (male speaker)","a":["ไม่เป็นไร","mâi-bpen-rai"],"o":["ขอโทษ","ขอบคุณ","สวัสดี"],"why":"ไม่เป็นไร means it's OK or never mind.","xr":["khǎaw-thôot","khàawp-khun","sà-wàt-dii"]},
      {"t":"type","p":"Thank you very much. (female speaker)","a":["ขอบคุณ มาก ค่ะ","ขอบคุณ มาก","khàawp-khun mâak khâ","khàawp-khun mâak"],"hint":"ขอบคุณ (khàawp-khun) · มาก (mâak) · ค่ะ (khâ)","x":["คะ"],"why":"A statement ends in ค่ะ, with a falling tone; คะ, with a high tone, asks a question.","xr":["khá"]},
      {"t":"type","p":"How are you? (male speaker)","a":["สบาย ดี ไหม ครับ","สบาย ดี ไหม","sà-baai dii mǎi khráp","sà-baai dii mǎi"],"hint":"สบาย (sà-baai) · ดี (dii) · ไหม (mǎi) · ครับ (khráp)","x":["ไม่"],"why":"ไหม (mǎi) with a rising tone asks the question; ไม่ (mâi), with a falling tone, means not.","xr":["mâi"]},
      {"t":"type","p":"Hello. (male speaker)","a":["สวัสดี ครับ","สวัสดี","sà-wàt-dii khráp","sà-wàt-dii"],"hint":"สวัสดี (sà-wàt-dii) · ครับ (khráp)","x":["ค่ะ"],"why":"A man ends with ครับ; ค่ะ is what women say.","xr":["khâ"]}
